    "checklist": {
      "reviewed": 6,
      "passRate": 48,
      "items": {
        "Balances are split into Current (not yet due) and past-due buckets of 1–30, 31–60, 61–90 and over 90 days, with no gaps or overlaps between ranges, and the page states whether days are counted from the due date or the invoice date": 0,
        "Each customer's row total equals the sum of its buckets, and a grand-total row, set apart from the customer rows, equals the sum of every bucket column and of the total column": 100,
        "An as-of date control is present, and the heading or a summary line states the as-of date, the currency, the total receivable and the total overdue (such as \"As of 31 Oct 2026 · VND\")": 0,
        "Money columns are right-aligned with fixed-width digits, thousand separators and one decimal convention, and credit balances such as overpayments carry a leading minus or brackets instead of being signalled by red text alone": 0,
        "Users can search by customer name or code, filter by at least one of salesperson, customer group or branch, and restrict the list to customers with overdue balances, with the number of customers shown": 100,
        "Each customer row expands, through a keyboard-operable control such as a button with aria-expanded, into its open invoices (invoice number, invoice date, due date, days overdue, open amount), and those amounts add up to the customer's row": 0,
        "Clicking a column header re-orders the customers and the header in use carries aria-sort; by default customers are ordered by their over-90 amount (or total balance), largest first": 100,
        "An Excel or CSV export is offered, and an @media print style removes navigation, filters and buttons while keeping the as-of date, column headings and grand total on paper": 0,
        "Filters that leave no balances show a message saying so instead of an empty grid or a row of zeros, and both a loading state and an error state with a retry action are built in": 100,
        "The slip identifies the employer (company name and tax code or address), the employee (full name, employee ID, department, job title) and the pay period together with its payment date": 100,
        "Earnings are itemised — basic salary with its proration (such as \"21 / 22 working days\"), each allowance, and overtime as hours × rate — and Gross pay equals the sum of the earnings lines": 0,
        "Deductions show the employee's social, health and unemployment insurance (each with its rate and contribution base) and personal income tax (with the taxable income it was computed on) apart from other deductions such as salary advances, and Total deductions equals their sum": 0,
        "Net pay equals Gross pay minus Total deductions to the last unit and is the most prominent figure on the slip": 100,
        "Amounts line up on the right with fixed-width digits and thousand separators, the currency is named, and decimals suit the currency (none for VND, two for USD) throughout": 100,
        "Earnings and deductions are marked up as tables with header cells or as dt/dd label–value pairs, so a screen reader announces each amount together with its label": 0,
        "A Print button is present, and the print stylesheet hides the app's sidebar, top bar and buttons, sets an A4 page with @page and keeps the earnings and deductions blocks from splitting across pages": 100,
        "The bank account number is masked except for its last four digits, and the slip carries a \"Confidential\" marking that also appears when printed": 0,
        "A period selector switches between months and the heading names the month shown; a month without a payslip shows a message saying so rather than zeros, and loading and error-with-retry states are built in": 0,
        "The day view lists rooms as rows, each labelled with its capacity (and its floor or equipment), against a time axis that covers working hours and is labelled at least every hour": 0,
        "A Day / Week switch marks the active view (aria-pressed, aria-selected or aria-current), Previous / Today / Next controls move the range, and a heading states the date or date range on screen (such as \"Mon 2 – Sun 8 Nov 2026\")": 100,
        "Each booking shows its title or organiser and its start–end time as text, and its block covers exactly that stretch of the time axis (a 09:30–11:00 booking spans one and a half hours)": 100,
        "Filters for minimum capacity and for equipment (such as projector or video conferencing) narrow the rooms listed, and the number of matching rooms is shown": 0,
        "Choosing a free slot opens a booking form already filled in with that room, date and start time": 100,
        "Saving is blocked with an inline message when the time overlaps another booking of the same room (the message names that booking's time and organiser) or when the end is not after the start": 100,
        "Cancelling a booking asks for confirmation in a dialog that names the room, date and time and offers a way to keep the booking": 100,
        "Free slots and bookings are focusable buttons or links whose accessible names give the room, date, time and status (such as \"Lotus room, Thu 5 Nov, 09:00–09:30, free\"), not click handlers on bare divs": 0,
        "When no rooms match the filters, a message with a clear-filters action takes the place of the grid, and loading and error-with-retry states are built in": 100,
        "Stage columns run in hiring order (such as Applied → Screening → Interview → Offer → Hired), and rejected or withdrawn candidates are kept out of the active columns, in a separate collapsed column or behind a filter": 100,
        "Each stage header shows a candidate count that matches the number of cards in that column under the current filters": 100,
        "The page names the opening being shown (job title, department, positions to fill and hired so far, such as \"Senior Accountant · Finance · 1 of 2 hired\"), and a selector switches to another opening": 0,
        "Each card gives the candidate's name, application source and days in the current stage, and candidates who have stayed past a stated limit are flagged with a text label or icon rather than colour alone": 0,
        "A card can change stage without dragging, through a \"Move to\" menu or buttons that work from the keyboard, and each move is announced through an aria-live region": 100,
        "Moving a candidate to Rejected opens a confirmation that names the candidate and requires a rejection reason before it completes": 100,
        "Search by candidate name or email and filters by source and by recruiter narrow the board, and the active filters are displayed with a way to clear them": 100,
        "Opening a card shows the candidate's contact details, a link to the CV and a stage history listing each move with its date and the person who made it": 0,
        "A stage with no candidates keeps its column and shows a placeholder such as \"No candidates\", and loading and error-with-retry states are built in": 100,
        "The hierarchy is an indented tree in which every unit with sub-units expands and collapses, exposed as role=\"tree\"/\"treeitem\" with aria-expanded (or nested lists whose toggles are buttons with aria-expanded) and operable from the keyboard": 100,
        "Each unit shows its total headcount including sub-units alongside its direct staff (such as \"42 · 8 direct\"), and every parent's total equals its direct staff plus its children's totals": 0,
        "Each unit names its manager, and a unit without one shows \"Vacant\" rather than a blank": 0,
        "The selected unit is marked in the tree (aria-selected or aria-current), and the details panel shows its name, code, path from the top (such as \"Company › Finance › Accounts Payable\"), manager and cost centre or location": 0,
        "The details panel compares approved positions with filled ones and gives vacancies as approved minus filled": 0,
        "The details panel lists the unit's direct employees with name and job title, and their number equals the unit's direct headcount": 0,
        "Searching by unit or manager name expands the ancestors of each match and highlights it, and a search with no match says so": 100,
        "Deactivating or moving a unit asks for confirmation in a dialog that names the unit and the number of employees and sub-units affected": 0,
        "A unit with no direct employees shows an explicit empty message in the details panel, and loading and error-with-retry states exist for both the tree and the panel": 0,
        "Each entry shows when, who (the person's name and account, or \"System\" or the integration's name for automated changes), the action, the affected record (type plus ID or name) and the outcome (such as Success, Failed or Denied) in text": 0,
        "Timestamps give the date and the time to the second with the time zone stated (such as \"05/11/2026 14:32:07 UTC+7\"), and entries are listed newest first": 0,
        "An update entry shows each changed field with its old and new value side by side under \"Before\" and \"After\" labels, so the change reads correctly without relying on colour": 0,
        "Passwords, tokens and other secret fields never appear in clear text; their changes are shown masked (such as \"•••••• changed\")": 0,
        "Filters cover a date range with presets, the actor, the action type and the record type, a search box finds a record by its ID, and the number of matching entries is shown": 100,
        "Entries are read-only: no edit or delete control appears on any entry, and the page states that the log cannot be altered": 100,
        "Export to CSV or Excel covers exactly the entries matching the current filters, and the export control states how many entries it will include": 0,
        "The log is a table with column header cells, and each entry's details open from a keyboard-operable control (a button with aria-expanded or a link) rather than only from a click on the row": 100,
        "Filters that match nothing show a message with a clear-filters action, and a loading state and an error state with retry are built in": 100
      }
    }
